  "description": "SCOUT's nodes in Curio. The Raster Calculator runs one operation over rasters on one grid: add, subtract, multiply, divide or choose, cell by cell, or a raster's statistics as a table of one row. Rasterize Buildings, SCOUT's building rasterizer ported from SCOUT (urban-toolkit/scout), turns a buildings layer into the zoom-16 height tiles SCOUT's Deep Umbra shadow model reads, side by side in one raster in metres that an Autark map draws. Fifteen Vega-Lite charts compare scenarios, one input per scenario: lines with a band, curves by group, bars with error bars, ensemble strips, stacked bars with totals, donuts, a weighted matrix, dots with a range, bars, grouped bars, lines, points, a pie, lollipops and a table. Each reads its inputs' rows stacked, each row named by the scenario box its input comes from, and draws each scenario in its box's color, in the order the dataflow lists the boxes; the columns it plots, and how it combines them, are widgets in its Widgets tab.",
  "id": "curio.scout",
  "license": "MIT",
  "name": "Scout",
  "permissions": [],
  "publisher": "Curio",
  "readOnly": true,
  "templates": [
    {
      "category": "computation",
      "description": "One operation over rasters on one grid. Connect the rasters to its input circles, in order; its code names the operation, with raster_calculate or raster_statistics from the package's scout_rasters.raster_algebra. Cell by cell: add, subtract, multiply or divide input_0 and input_1, or choose, which takes input_1 where input_0's class is one of the codes it names and input_2 elsewhere; a cell that is nodata in an input the operation reads there is nodata in the result, and rasters on different grids are refused; absolute=True gives the size of the result, such as how much a depth changed. Statistics: the mean, median, minimum, maximum and count of a raster's cells, nodata left out; its code can keep only the cells that meet a condition, such as a value under 1.08, on the raster itself or on a second raster on input_1, on the same grid, used as a mask: a test of the mask's values or a set of them. An input may be a layer instead, which the code reads as zones or a mask, for example rasterized on a raster's grid, or a JSON value the code reads as it is, such as the corners of a region a node wired into it returns. The output is the result: a raster an Autark map draws, or the statistics as a table of one row, which this package's charts draw for each scenario.",
      "editor": "code",
      "engine": "python",
      "hasCode": true,
      "hasGrammar": false,
      "hasWidgets": true,
      "iconRef": "fa-solid:calculator",
      "id": "raster-calculator",
      "inputPorts": [
        {
          "cardinality": "[1,3]",
          "types": [
            "RASTER",
            "GEODATAFRAME",
            "JSON"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "label": "Raster Calculator",
      "behavior": "code",
      "outputPorts": [
        {
          "cardinality": "1",
          "types": [
            "RASTER",
            "DATAFRAME"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "paletteOrder": 0,
      "source": "sources/raster-calculator.py",
      "dataflowCategories": {
        "dataTypes": [
          "Rasters"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "category": "computation",
      "description": "SCOUT's OSM vector to raster: draws each building's height into 256 by 256 map tiles at a zoom level, 8-bit gray where 255 is the maximum height, in EPSG:3395. Input: a buildings GeoDataFrame with a column of heights in metres. Output: one RASTER of the tiles side by side, heights in metres, band band_1, for an Autark map and for Accumulated Shadow (model.scout.deep-umbra), which runs SCOUT's Deep Umbra shadow model on it. A tile SCOUT writes no file for, because no building is near it, is no data.",
      "editor": "code",
      "engine": "python",
      "hasCode": true,
      "hasGrammar": false,
      "hasWidgets": true,
      "iconRef": "fa-solid:city",
      "id": "rasterize-buildings",
      "inputPorts": [
        {
          "cardinality": "1",
          "types": [
            "GEODATAFRAME"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "label": "Rasterize Buildings",
      "behavior": "code",
      "outputPorts": [
        {
          "cardinality": "1",
          "types": [
            "RASTER"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "paletteOrder": 1,
      "source": "sources/rasterize-buildings.py",
      "widgets": [
        {
          "name": "attribute",
          "type": "text",
          "label": "Height column",
          "default": "height"
        },
        {
          "name": "zoom",
          "type": "number",
          "label": "Zoom level",
          "default": 16,
          "options": {
            "min": 1,
            "max": 20,
            "step": 1
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "max_height",
          "type": "number",
          "label": "Maximum height",
          "default": 550,
          "options": {
            "min": 1,
            "step": 1,
            "units": "m"
          }
        }
      ],
      "dataflowCategories": {
        "dataTypes": [
          "Rasters"
        ]
      }
    },
